{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795042783,"nonce":"B1ulHa8sTI7ngPfySNOmHFXaf34=","message":"Follow-up reviewed on local main e428e226 (2026-11-18).\nSource: https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/issues/79#issuecomment-6992562692\n\nThe follow-up extends this issue to tooltip, popover, alert-dialog and toast semantics. It requests Tooltip, Dialog, AlertDialog, Status, Alert and Region roles. Toast and status updates also need live regions, which announce changed content to assistive technology. The existing menu, menubar, separator, tree, treeitem, toolbar and distinct checkbox/radio menu-item requirements still apply. Dialog initial focus remains separate: #82 is implemented, pushed and closed through e428e226.\n\nRead-only source audit\n\nThe role enum and renderer mapping still contain the reported gaps. Date Picker and picker popovers already declare role=dialog, but the mapper drops it. The tooltip, popover, dialog/alert-dialog and toast builders do not set the requested content roles. AccessibilityNode has no live-region properties, and no aria-live/aria-atomic/aria-relevant handling was found in crates or extensions. Desktop still has no semantic-snapshot consumer.\n\nThere is an additional traversal risk. accessibility_nodes stops descending after it emits a recognized role. Adding Dialog, Menu, Tree or Region without changing that rule will omit child controls. Preserve grouping and child order for container roles while keeping atomic controls, such as labelled buttons and checkboxes, as single accessible controls.\n\nThe snapshot's focused field currently comes from editable-widget bindings. Adapter work must also expose the event router's current focus for buttons and menu items, using stable IDs. The new #82 routing supplies that focus but does not itself publish a desktop accessibility tree.\n\nImplementation order and acceptance criteria\n\n1. Extend shared semantic roles and preserve container descendants. Keep checkbox/radio menu-item variants distinct. Cover names, checked/selected/expanded/disabled state, stable identities and focus.\n2. Add live-region metadata and change tracking. Define announcement behavior for additions, updates and removals. Repainting an unchanged toast must not announce it again. Respect the selected announcement priority and atomic content behavior.\n3. Set appropriate semantic roles in CN builders. Cover tooltip, popover, dialog, alert dialog, toast and existing picker dialogs. Keep role selection separate from appearance and focus behavior.\n4. Deliver the shared semantics, focus updates, assistive actions and live announcements through the desktop adapter. Updating only the enum or setting role attributes does not complete #79.\n5. Add scoped semantic/component tests and adapter checks. Preserve the existing iOS mapping when roles expand. Keep native screen-reader validation distinct from compilation and snapshot tests. The reporter offered Orca/Linux and NVDA/Windows testing, but no coordination message was sent.\n\nThis is a review and scope update. No Rust source changed and no build or test gate ran. Keep this track OPEN. The plan remains in git-bug. No new Markdown plan, source commit, push or GitHub comment in this step.","files":null}]}